iption":"Show theseus CLI help"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GFHvMenPHTpAYxTj54mURS","tool_input":{"command":"sed -n '1817,4329p' DocService/sources/DocsCoServer.js | grep -nE \"^  (async )?function |^  function\\*|^  const [a-zA-Z]+ = |^  [a-zA-Z.]+\\.on\\(|case '|^  [a-z]+\\(\" | awk -F: '{print $1+1816\": \"$2$3}' | head -200","description":"List nested functions and handlers inside install()"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011UKdMb1ChSdTwCWHSCN4wA","tool_input":{"command":"sed -n '2787,3300p' DocService/sources/DocsCoServer.js | grep -nE \"yield|await|connections\\.push|return\" | grep -vE \"ctx\\.getCfg|^\\s*$\" | head -90","description":"Skim key async steps in auth/endAuth"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01VcNhFmMwr68BRrr4XfuxjM","tool_input":{"command":"theseus validate","description":"Run theseus validation before changes"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_018R7VoEJ8kcvyR5AWUSqSmb","tool_input":{"command":"file -L /root/.local/bin/theseus; head -5 /root/.local/bin/theseus","description":"Inspect theseus CLI entry script"}},{"tool_name":"Read","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NYm9ASLRk9gKSKp4nBxwNw","tool_input":{"file_path":"/root/.local/bin/theseus","limit":20}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01HLwV2EHxxeh1byLUA9E6ws","tool_input":{"command":"grep -rnE \"require\\([^)]*['/]database['\\\")]\" --include=*.js . | grep -v node_modules; sed -n '/^---$/,$p' .theseus/atlas/docservice.md | sed '1,/^---$/d' | wc -w","description":"Check database.js callers and body word count"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01A9kv1kV3caq17XX8Hrmtjj","tool_input":{"command":"theseus validate","description":"Acceptance: run theseus validate"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01G91pcBvmBZCs9ULdW9nDUH","tool_input":{"command":"git add .theseus/atlas/docservice.md && git commit -q -m \"docs(atlas): add DocService module card (PKT-0003)\n\nMap the DocService package: entry points, connection/auth/edit/save/close\nflows of DocsCoServer.js, invariants, pitfalls (circular requires, module\nstate, closures inside install), oracle gaps and a proposed submodule split.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GfMVS4GJ2FBm26wB5X9Aot\" && git log --oneline -1 && git status --short","description":"Commit the Atlas card"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vi76iEWtn52tViiZuW9bxC","tool_input":{"command":"git add .theseus/atlas/docservice.md","description":"Stage the Atlas card"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":38,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the DocService Atlas card, but it isn't committed and `theseus validate` didn't run. In this session `git add`, `git commit` and every `theseus` command need approval I couldn't get. So the file `.theseus/atlas/docservice.md` exists but is uncommitted. Of the two acceptance commands, only `test -f .theseus/atlas/docservice.md` ran, and it passed.\n\nTo finish, run from the worktree:\n```bash\ntheseus validate\ngit add .theseus/atlas/docservice.md\ngit commit -m \"docs(atlas): add DocService module card (PKT-0003)\"\n```\n\n## What the card covers\n- **What it is:** an Express + socket.io server that coordinates co-editing. It handles connections, presence, locks, storing changes, saving and the callbacks to the host app, plus the conversion, download and WOPI endpoints. It doesn't convert files itself: it sends that work to FileConverter over RabbitMQ.\n- **Entry points:** `server.js`, `DocsCoServer.install`, `commandFromServer`, and the main functions of canvasservice, converterservice, wopiClient, the database connectors and editorDataMemory.\n- **`DocsCoServer.js` flows:** startup order; connecting (`io.use` checks the token); `auth` → `endAuth`; editing (`getLock` / `saveChanges` / `publish`); closing (`closeDocument` → save timer → `saveFromChanges` → FileConverter → `receiveTask` → callback); and two background timers (session expiry and WOPI lock refresh).\n- **Tests:** none for the core. `DocsCoServer.js`, `canvasservice.js`, `converterservice.js` and `wopiClient.js` have no unit tests, and any refactor needs a `characterize` packet first.\n- **Proposed split** under \"Open questions\": seven `coserver/*` parts carved out of `DocsCoServer.js`, plus canvas, converter, wopi and storage.\n\n## Decisions\n- **Metric fields left empty.** Size, languages, dependencies and metrics are `null`, because the spec says only tools fill them and no tool output exists. The line counts in the text come from the packet itself.\n- **Index not regenerated.** `INDEX.md` says it is generated from the cards and must not be edited by hand, and I couldn't run the CLI to regenerate it.\n- **Friction not written.** `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl` is outside `create_in`, so I left it alone. The entries are below so they can be added.\n- **Claims tagged `[model]`.** Every claim in the card carries that tag; the card has no reviewer yet.\n\n## Lessons for the Atlas\n- `install()` is about half of `DocsCoServer.js`, and most handlers are functions defined inside it, which is the main reason it can't be unit-tested.\n- Six files require `DocsCoServer`, and it requires them back (circular dependencies).\n- `changes2forgotten.js` is a standalone script that shuts the process down when loaded, so the server must never require it.\n- The default editor-state storage (`editorDataMemory`) keeps everything in memory in a single process. This repo has no other backend for running several nodes.\n- Grep found no code that requires `database.js`, so it may be dead code (listed as an open question).\n\n## Friction to record\n- **Missing step:** `investigate` packets have no step or command to regenerate `INDEX.md`, and `.theseus/atlas/INDEX.md` sits inside `create_in`, so it's unclear whether the executor should touch it.\n- **Rule conflict:** the executor prompt (step 8) says to append to `friction.jsonl`, but that file is outside this packet's `create_in`.\n- **Environment:** acceptance requires `theseus validate`, but the executor's sandbox couldn't run it, and couldn't run `git add`/`git commit` either.\n\nNo packets were spawned.","ttft_ms":3120,"type":"result","duration_ms":146314,"uuid":"0918a27b-1941-4414-8879-dfa5fe81c5c4","ttft_stream_ms":1768,"time_to_request_ms":322,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":176,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":22,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":7,"engine_pickup":7,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":14,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":26,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":4,"request_build":13},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":58,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":164,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":212,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":138,"process_rss_mib_result":235,"process_anon_mib_result":144,"process_peak_rss_mib":259,"process_cpu_ms_turn":4502,"process_wall_ms_turn":146313,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":2070,"process_wall_ms_streaming":97000,"main_stream_count":28,"main_stream_event_count":1681,"main_stream_chunk_count":1197,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":10,"cpu_ms":22,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":9,"ambient_wait_ms":9,"render_ms":